is Hölder-continuous and the metric $\omega+dd^{c}\varphi$ has cone singularities along $D$.","arxiv_id":"1104.4879","theorem_id":"Theorem B"},{"title":"Regularisation of Currents with Mass Control and Singular Morse Inequalities","theorem":"Let $T\geq\gamma$ be a $d$-closed current of bidegree $(1,\,1)$ on a compact complex manifold $X$, where $\gamma$ is a continuous $(1,\,1)$-form such that $d\gamma=0$. Then, in the $\partial\bar{\partial}$-cohomology class of $T$, there exist closed $(1,\,1)$-currents $T_{m}$ with analytic singularities converging to $T$ in the weak topology of currents such that each $T_{m}$ is smooth on $X\setminus V{\mathcal{I}}(mT)$ and: 



