Let $T\geq\gamma$ be a $d$-closed current of bidegree $(1,\,1)$ on a compact complex manifold $X$, where $\gamma$ is a continuous $(1,\,1)$-form such that $d\gamma=0$. Then, in the $\partial\bar{\partial}$-cohomology class of $T$, there exist closed $(1,\,1)$-currents $T_{m}$ with analytic singularities converging to $T$ in the weak topology of currents such that each $T_{m}$ is smooth on $X\setminus V{\mathcal{I}}(mT)$ and: 



$(a)$   $\displaystyle T_{m}\geq\gamma-\frac{C}{m}\,\omega$,     $m\in\mathbb{N}$; 



$(b)$   $\displaystyle\nu(T,\,x)-\varepsilon_{m}\leq\nu(T_{m},\,x)\leq\nu(T,\,x),\hskip 8.61108ptx\in X,\,m\in\mathbb{N}$, for some $\varepsilon_{m}\downarrow 0$; 



$(c)$   $\displaystyle\lim\limits_{m\rightarrow+\infty}\frac{1}{m}\,\int\limits_{X\setminus V{\mathcal{I}}(mT)}(T_{m}-\gamma+\frac{C}{m}\,\omega)^{k}\wedge\omega^{n-k}=0$,     $k=1,\dots,\,n=\mbox{dim}_{\mathbb{C}}X$, 



where $\omega$ is an arbitrary Hermitian metric on $X$.

For arbitrary $\eta=(\eta_{1},\ldots,\eta_{p})\in(0,+\infty)^{p},$ the function



$M_{\eta}(t_{1},\ldots,t_{p})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{p}}\max\{t_{1}+h_{1},\ldots,t_{p}+h_{p}\}\prod_{1\leq j\leq p}\theta\left(\frac{h_{j}}{\eta_{j}}\right)dh_{1}\ldots dh_{p}$



possesses the following properties:


$(1)$ $M_{\eta}(t_{1},\ldots,t_{p})$ is non decreasing in all variables, smooth and convex on $\mathbb{R}^{p}$;


$(2)$ $\max\{t_{1},\ldots,t_{p}\}\leq M_{\eta}(t_{1},\ldots,t_{p})\leq\max\{t_{1}+\eta_{1},\ldots,t_{p}+\eta_{p}\}$;


$(3)$ $M_{\eta}(t_{1},\ldots,t_{p})=M_{(\eta_{1},\ldots,\hat{\eta}_{j},\ldots,\eta_{p})}(t_{1},\ldots,\hat{t}_{j},\ldots,t_{p})$ if $t_{j}+\eta_{j}\leq\max_{k\not=j}\{t_{k}-\eta_{k}\}$;


$(4)$ $M_{\eta}(t_{1}+a,\ldots,t_{p}+a)=M_{\eta}(t_{1},\ldots,t_{p})+a$ for any $a\in\mathbb{R}$;


$(5)$ if $u_{1},\ldots,u_{p}$ are plurisubharmonic functions, then $u=M_{\eta}(u_{1},\ldots,u_{p})$ is plurisubharmonic.
